---
import { siteConfig } from '../../config/site';
---

<section id="about" style="padding:6rem 0;background-color:#F5F1E8;">
  <div style="max-width:1200px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 2rem;">
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(300px,1fr));gap:4rem;align-items:start;">

      <!-- Photo + credentials -->
      <div class="fade-left">
        <div style="position:relative;border-radius:0.25rem;overflow:hidden;box-shadow:0 2px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.09);">
          <img
            src="/images/about/headshot.jpg"
            alt="Elan Green, MSW, LSWAIC - Therapist at Liminal Oak Therapy"
            width="600"
            height="450"
            style="width:100%;height:auto;display:block;"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </div>

        <div style="margin-top:2rem;">
          <p style="font-family:'Josefin Sans',sans-serif;font-size:0.875rem;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:0.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D5A3D;margin-bottom:1rem;">
            Credentials
          </p>
          <ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0;border-top:1px solid rgba(74,55,40,0.1);">
            <li style="padding:0.875rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(74,55,40,0.1);">
              <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;font-weight:500;color:#4A3728;font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;">BS, Psychology</p>
              <p style="font-size:0.8125rem;font-family:'Josefin Sans',sans-serif;letter-spacing:0.06em;color:#6B5B4E;margin-top:0.2rem;">Bachelor of Science · University of Washington</p>
            </li>
            <li style="padding:0.875rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(74,55,40,0.1);">
              <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;font-weight:500;color:#4A3728;font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;">MSW</p>
              <p style="font-size:0.8125rem;font-family:'Josefin Sans',sans-serif;letter-spacing:0.06em;color:#6B5B4E;margin-top:0.2rem;">Master of Social Work · University of Washington</p>
            </li>
            <li style="padding:0.875rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(74,55,40,0.1);">
              <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;font-weight:500;color:#4A3728;font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;">LSWAIC</p>
              <p style="font-size:0.8125rem;font-family:'Josefin Sans',sans-serif;letter-spacing:0.06em;color:#6B5B4E;margin-top:0.2rem;">Licensed Social Worker Associate &ndash; Independent Clinical &middot; SWIA.SC.61683693</p>
            </li>
            <li style="padding:0.875rem 0;">
              <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;font-weight:500;color:#4A3728;font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;">Psychedelic Researcher</p>
              <p style="font-size:0.8125rem;font-family:'Josefin Sans',sans-serif;letter-spacing:0.06em;color:#6B5B4E;margin-top:0.2rem;">
                <a href="https://ntap.psychiatry.uw.edu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#2D5A3D;">Center for Novel Therapeutics in Addictive Psychiatry</a> &middot; University of Washington &middot; 4 years
              </p>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Bio -->
      <div class="fade-right">
        <p style="font-family:'Josefin Sans',sans-serif;font-size:0.875rem;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:0.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D5A3D;margin-bottom:1.25rem;">
          About
        </p>
        <h2 style="font-size:2rem;font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;color:#4A3728;margin-bottom:2rem;line-height:1.3;font-weight:500;">
          Hi, I&rsquo;m Elan.
        </h2>

        <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:1.5rem;">
          <p style="font-size:1.125rem;color:#4A3728;line-height:1.8;">
            Many people come to me having already tried a great deal: talk therapy, medication, the books and the videos. They&rsquo;ve worked hard and still feel stuck, caught somewhere between who they&rsquo;ve been and who they&rsquo;re becoming.
          </p>
          <p style="font-size:1.125rem;color:#4A3728;line-height:1.8;">
            That space between is where I work. I don&rsquo;t believe healing is about fixing what&rsquo;s broken; it&rsquo;s about rediscovering a wholeness that trauma, shame, and conditional love have buried but never erased. My approach moves from the ground up: first building safety and steadiness in the nervous system, then using the body as a map to surface and unburden what has been stored there, and finally opening toward meaning, purpose, and what becomes possible when the weight lifts.
          </p>
          <p style="font-size:1.125rem;color:#4A3728;line-height:1.8;">
            I also specialize in psychedelic preparation and integration. Drawing on four years as a psychedelic researcher at the University of Washington, I offer grounded, clinically informed support for those preparing for or making meaning of a psychedelic experience, whether in a clinical trial, a retreat, or a personal context.
          </p>
          <p style="font-size:1.125rem;color:#4A3728;line-height:1.8;">
            My name, Elan, means &ldquo;oak tree&rdquo; in Hebrew. Like the oak, I believe we grow strongest when we&rsquo;re deeply rooted: connected to our bodies, our stories, and something larger than ourselves.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>
